#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install snap on CentOS 7, 8, or 9 Stream using EPEL, resolve "
"missing dependencies, and enable the socket and classic support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:8
msgid "Install snap on CentOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:10
msgid ""
"Snap is available for [CentOS 9 Stream](https://www.centos.org/), CentOS 8 "
"Stream, CentOS 8 and CentOS 7, from the 7.6 release onwards. It's also "
"available for Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) 7.6+ (see {ref}`Installing "
"snap on Red Hat Enterprise Linux <interfaces-installing-snap-on-red-hat>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:12
msgid ""
"The packages for CentOS 8/9 and CentOS 7 are in each distribution's "
"respective [Extra Packages for Enterprise Linux](https://fedoraproject.org/"
"wiki/EPEL) (EPEL) repository. The instructions for adding this repository "
"diverge slightly between CentOS 8/9 and CentOS 7, which is why they're "
"listed separately below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:15
msgid ""
"If you need to know which version of CentOS you're running, type `cat /etc/"
"centos-release`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:18
msgid ""
"If you don't already have the EPEL repository added to your distribution, it "
"can be added as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:20
msgid "CentOS 8/9 Stream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:22
msgid ""
"The EPEL repository can be added to a CentOS 8/9 Stream system with the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:24
msgid ""
"sudo dnf install epel-release\n"
"sudo dnf upgrade\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:29
msgid "CentOS 7 Stream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:31
msgid ""
"The EPEL repository can be added to a CentOS 7 system with the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:33
msgid "sudo yum install epel-release\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:37
msgid "Missing packages with EPEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:39
msgid ""
"Packages in the EPEL repository are built against dependencies from the "
"current RHEL release, and these packages are regularly imported from RHEL by "
"the CentOS project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:41
msgid ""
"Occasionally, however, the exact version of a specific package used to build "
"the snapd RPM has yet to be imported into the base CentOS repositories. This "
"can cause missing package errors similar to the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:43
msgid ""
"Problem: package snapd-2.42.1-1.el8.x86_64 requires snapd-selinux = "
"2.42.1-1.el8,\n"
"but none of the providers can be installed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:48
msgid ""
"In such an event, rather than waiting for EPEL packages to be updated, you "
"can enable the [continuous release (CR)](<https://wiki.centos.org/"
"AdditionalResources(2f)Repositories(2f)CR.html>) repository. This repository "
"contains packages destined for the next point release of CentOS and should "
"satisfy any missing version mismatch dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:50
msgid ""
"If you're interested in understanding how these packages are built, see  "
"{ref}`Building a snap RPM for Red Hat Enterprise Linux <interfaces-building-"
"snap-rpms-on-rhel>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:52
msgid "Installing snapd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:54
msgid ""
"With the EPEL repository added to your CentOS installation, simply install "
"the *snapd* package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:56
msgid "sudo yum install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:60
msgid ""
"Once installed, the *systemd* unit that manages the main snap communication "
"socket needs to be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:62
msgid "sudo systemctl enable --now snapd.socket\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:66
msgid ""
"To enable *classic* snap support, enter the following to create a symbolic "
"link between `/var/lib/snapd/snap` and `/snap`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:68
msgid "sudo ln -s /var/lib/snapd/snap /snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/centos.md:72
msgid ""
"Either log out and back in again or restart your system to ensure snap’s "
"paths are updated correctly."
msgstr ""
